{"agent_id":"pp3g-REr3-adversarial-review-of-the-b1-b6-remediation-plan-9b2e","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-08-14T21:47:42.737565619Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"0658e85d-4f1c-4e1e-9383-46c5cb6eadf4","comment_uuid":"f084bf6b-2f9a-41cb-a97a-bf984f284c62","author":"pp3g-REr3-adversarial-review-of-the-b1-b6-remediation-plan-9b2e","content":"# ADVERSARIAL REVIEW — Remediation Plan B1-B6 (#361)\n\nReviewer: mimo-v2.5 (independent, zero-context). Date: 2026-08-14.\n\n## Review Summary: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe plan is well-structured and grounded in verified evidence. The three-class rules ownership map (B1), the drop of .ases/ (B2), the re-sequencing of step 5 (B4), and the contract battery (B6) are sound. However, three blocking design flaws must be addressed before implementation.\n\n## MUST FIX (blocking)\n\n### BF-1: B3 enforcement check has no failure-mode definition\n\nThe plan proposes a startup marker check in crosslink-guard.ts but defines warn-mode and hard-fail without specifying what happens when the check ITSELF fails (manifest missing, corrupted, unreadable). Three undefined states: (1) fail open = drift undetected, (2) fail closed = wedges every session, (3) warn = weakened enforcement. The plan says hard-fail after sync proven but never defines proven operationally.\n\nFix: Define three explicit states. State 0 (pre-sync): no manifest = no-op. State 1 (warn-mode): manifest exists, mismatch logged, no hard-fail. State 2 (hard-fail): manifest exists AND sync-tooling.sh --check run successfully at least once. Transition = deliberate operator action (e.g. --promote flag), not automatic.\n\n### BF-2: B5 step-0 commit mixes concerns\n\nStep 0 commits Tools uncommitted scripts/claude + .crosslink/rules/global.md. But global.md is layer-owned per B1s own classification. Committing it to Tools contradicts the ownership map: you cannot say rules are layer-owned and not synced while committing a layer-owned rules file to Tools. The global.md delta should be stashed, not committed. B5 local-edit preservation should SKIP it.\n\n### BF-3: B5 transaction log creates state-management burden with no rollback for the rollback\n\nThe plan introduces Tools/.sync-state/ and Tools/.sync-backup/ — two new mutable state stores. The transaction log can itself become corrupted (partial JSON write on crash). The backup directory is in Tools (the source, not destination) — should be in destination git history. No second-level rollback if the restored version is broken.\n\nFix: Drop the transaction log. Rely on git for atomicity: script writes files, operator commits in each destination repo. Drop backup directory: git history IS the backup. Make script idempotent (always overwrite, never skip).,","created_at":"2026-08-14T21:47:42.728953622Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:kaf/Oz7c6BWiav0zvdNqtVCp7+iJfoP07LfEx10tSuE","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgw+l+JOUUy3CnHlQfwhto47tVC9UsslHD++zIZePOaSMAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAvelwwkAm+clQwV194uJJ+sCywo70LpL/dIm5Umr0xD33vi8nidBj+EALI09DT+Nv46M7Kf1VjtXCg97R6SeCBg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:kaf/Oz7c6BWiav0zvdNqtVCp7+iJfoP07LfEx10tSuE","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgw+l+JOUUy3CnHlQfwhto47tVC9UsslHD++zIZePOaSMAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJbbo+pRphEXAo0RyFB0weI3L591jk1LpOlGZ+Fbf4o+uGkxLyf1KcfyqVERZm+3x6MB5kXWOrMIc83h9a7RNAo="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-REr3-adversarial-review-of-the-b1-b6-remediation-plan-9b2e","agent_seq":3,"timestamp":"2026-08-14T21:47:58.723949024Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"0658e85d-4f1c-4e1e-9383-46c5cb6eadf4","comment_uuid":"b7282278-cba1-4eba-945f-118edf6e60d5","author":"pp3g-REr3-adversarial-review-of-the-b1-b6-remediation-plan-9b2e","content":"## SHOULD CONSIDER (non-blocking)\n\n### NC-1: B3 sync-tooling.sh --check is a preflight, not a consumer check\n\nThe plan conflates two concerns: (1) consumer-side check (startup, every session) = guard plugin marker comparison, and (2) preflight check (on demand, before deploy) = sync-tooling.sh --check. These serve different purposes. Preflight catches drift before deployment; consumer check catches drift after. Should be explicitly distinguished.\n\n### NC-2: B6 contract battery requires runtime deps not available in scratch dirs\n\nItems 1 (--agent), 5 (fork identity), 8 (plugin contract) require opencode, fork binary, bun/ts runtime. A scratch dir wont have these. Battery should run in LIVE environment where dependencies exist, or explicitly list prerequisites with a setup script.\n\n### NC-3: B4 step 5 ASES mirror is second simultaneous cutover\n\nPlan says mirror the same pinned sequence in ASES — two repos cutovered in same step. If Tools succeeds but ASES fails, asymmetric hook versions. Should sequence explicitly: Tools first, verify, then ASES.\n\n### NC-4: B1 md5 count is a snapshot\n\n28/31 identical is true TODAY but changes on binary rebuild. The ownership map (not the count) is the durable artifact. Should document this.\n\n### NC-5: sync-tooling.sh maintenance and deployment undefined\n\nPlan describes what it does but not where it lives, how deployed, who maintains, how versioned. The sync tool is itself a piece of tooling needing canonical-source treatment.\n\n### NC-6: B3 D1 workflow inversion fix is incomplete\n\nPlan says consumer check fixes D1 inversion explicitly. But check only detects drift — the actual fix requires bidirectional sync capability in sync-tooling.sh. Should state that D1 is resolved by the scripts bidirectional capability, not just the consumer check.\n\n## NITS\n\n### N-1: B5 atomic staging via *.sync-tmp rename is fragile\nIf process crashes between write and rename, orphaned temp files. Simpler: write directly, rely on git for atomicity.\n\n### N-2: B6 contract battery item 4 should test literal-quote bug specifically\nShould include test case: prompt with spaces+special chars, verify ONE argument to opencode.\n\n### N-3: Risk register R10 underspecified\nhook-config.json divergence: ASES has comment_discipline=encouraged/signing_enforcement=audit, tripn has required/enforced. Guard behavior differs. Plan documents but does not prescribe resolution.","created_at":"2026-08-14T21:47:58.711576225Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:kaf/Oz7c6BWiav0zvdNqtVCp7+iJfoP07LfEx10tSuE","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgw+l+JOUUy3CnHlQfwhto47tVC9UsslHD++zIZePOaSMAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAm/6jazzvT3dIctkfZv/j69HFql1NreCP7NUugbF5Ee+B7zeiwIDOulD3jZ1HL51nZFKV6ajdr0GQyPu5INBeBQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:kaf/Oz7c6BWiav0zvdNqtVCp7+iJfoP07LfEx10tSuE","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgw+l+JOUUy3CnHlQfwhto47tVC9UsslHD++zIZePOaSMAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQK2X6hw1bDV1G5iw1PtH8aca6vjypx7k/3y5WcndNyQQu4oxjKQ8zrA2nGnLqsabZFE+ow7Hy/sKxugE/isnxQM="}
